+  //! Two stripes A (the earlier) and B whose blends overlap on face F and
+  //! cannot be made one (their recomputation overflowing F failed): A is
+  //! computed again on the faces of its edge, and B rolls on A's contact
+  //! line on F (its ball touches B's other face and passes through that
+  //! line; F vanishes between them). Returns false when either fails.
